# Amazon Inspector ignore list for drillapi
# Used by aws-actions/vulnerability-scan-github-action-for-amazon-inspector
# (invoked via SFOE-prometheon/github-terraform-workflows ecr-build-scan-push.yml)
#
# Every entry below is a third-party OS package or embedded binary inside the
# AWS Lambda base image public.ecr.aws/lambda/python:3.14 (AL2023), or the
# dev-only Alpine image. None are vulnerabilities in drillapi's own code, and
# none are patchable by us directly — all are blocked on upstream (AWS's AL2023
# repo, or the curl/rpm/glibc/aws-lambda-rie maintainers) shipping a fixed
# package. `dnf upgrade --refresh` is already run in Dockerfile.lambda; re-check
# it on every dependency bump and remove an entry once a patch actually lands.
#
# Full verification methodology (exact commands run, raw output, filesystem
# checks) is intentionally kept out of this public file to avoid publishing a
# ready-made reconnaissance map alongside a public base image. The complete
# writeup is maintained privately as a draft GitHub Security Advisory:
# GHSA-9gx6-3c8f-2873 (repo collaborators only — not public, not published).

